```

---

## 📋 Chatbot Features Implemented [1]

The chatbot implements the ICA conversational assistant pattern from the implementation guide [1]:

| Feature | Implemented |
|---|---|
| **Welcome message** | ✅ Explains what can be inspected and what cannot be changed |
| **Logical question order** | ✅ Objective → System → Release → Business Action → Evidence → Analysis Type |
| **Simple choices** | ✅ ABAP / SU24 / OData / Combined options with buttons |
| **Confirmation screen** | ✅ "You are asking us to inspect X in system Y using evidence Z" |
| **Readable findings** | ✅ Severity, confidence, evidence reference, recommendation |
| **Request ID tracking** | ✅ Unique ID generated for audit trail |
| **Safety warnings** | ✅ Diagnostic and read-only, human approval required |
| **Approval workflow** | ✅ Routes findings to SAP Security before action |

---

## ⚠️ Important Reminders

This chatbot is based on the IBM Bob + ICA + MCP Gateway implementation guide [1]:

> **"The first release must be diagnostic and read-only. It must not directly change SAP roles, SU24, ABAP code, OData configuration or production data. Any change must go through the existing human approval and change-management process."** [1]

All findings from this chatbot **require human SAP Security approval** before any correction is applied [1].

---

## 🚀 Next Steps for Production Use

To deploy this in your project with the full implementation guide [1]:

